WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.320
You know what they used to do to guys like
that when they were in a place like this?

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.399
They'd be carried out on a stretcher, folks.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.540
I'm gonna stomp all over your face with golf
spikes

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:11.380
because I'm gonna win this for the state of
Pennsylvania.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:17.300
You cannot be civil with a political party
that wants to destroy

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.220
what you stand for, what you care about.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:23.800
If politics these days seem especially ugly,
that's because they are.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.920
Not even counting physical attacks on Senator
Rand Paul,

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.140
the shooting of Congressman Steve Scalise

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.820
and the punching and kicking that have become
routine at demonstrations

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:36.500
politics are more heated and divisive than
they've been in years.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.620
And for good reason, the people who control
politics

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:43.440
insist that every piece of legislation, every
supreme court nomination,

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.600
every midterm election, every minor rule change

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.800
is bringing the world one step closer to the
apocalypse.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:54.040
Using plastic straws, kneeling for the national
anthem, decade old tweets.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:56.100
There isn't anything we do anymore

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.900
that doesn't immediately get sucked into angry
partisan arguments.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:04.140
Civility won't return until more of us channel
our inner libertarians

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.940
and realize that not all parts of our lives
need to be politicized.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:09.640
How do you expect people to respond

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:13.140
when we're told each day is the beginning
of the end of our way of life,

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:16.020
that the other side is not just mistaken but
pure evil-

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:21.920
You are either complicit in the evil, you
are either contributing to the wrong

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.680
or you are fighting against it.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:27.040
And we're limited to two parties that represent
fewer and fewer of us.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:30.080
The government is spending more, it's borrowing
more

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:34.900
and it's controlling more and more aspects
of our lives for no reason other than pure political gain.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:40.060
If we are fortunate enough two win back the
House and/or the Senate.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:42.260
That's when civility can start again.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:47.700
If civility can't return to politics unless
your team is in charge, you're doing it wrong.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:53.240
Civility is only going to return when people
stop treating politics as the only thing that matters

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:57.240
and we start actually shrinking the size,
scope and spending of government

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.440
and give ourselves some room to breathe.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:02.720
That's especially true if we're stuck with
just two choices

00:02:02.729 --> 00:02:04.890
who have pledged to screw the other side over.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:09.960
Neither Republicans nor Democrats offer a
plan where you get to live however you want.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:14.140
Which helps explain why so few of us want
to be part of either party.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:16.880
And why civility won't return to politics

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:21.680
until politicians stop cramming themselves
into every corner of our lives.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:27.580
Lock her up! Lock her up! Lock her up! Lock
her up!

